+
+## Validation and real exits
+
+- Required initial `set_status(..., analysis)`: exit 0.
+- Tool readiness (`command -v task-board`, `task-board --help`): exit 0.
+- First compact board query: exit 1 on unsupported `acceptanceCriteria`; scoped
+  `schema(operation=get)`: exit 0; corrected compact projections: exit 0.
+- `task-board validate --json` current authoritative board: exit 0 with
+  `valid=true`, empty errors, and empty warnings.
+- First contract-check attempt: exit 1 because its literal token matcher did not
+  normalize a Markdown line break. Corrected whitespace-normalized contract
+  checker: exit 0, nine exact required checks and three rejecting validator
+  result shapes.
+- `plantuml -checkonly`: exit 0.
+- PlantUML SVG render and non-empty check: exit 0.
+- Temporary PNG render for visual inspection: exit 0; layout and updated runner
+  boundary were manually inspected. Direct SVG image-view attempt failed as
+  unsupported by the runtime viewer; this is distinct from the successful SVG
+  parse/render.
+- `git diff --check`: exit 0.
+- `scripts/tests/test-credential-free-validation.sh`: exit 1. The unchanged
+  script expects deferred `ReluxProxyIOSUITests`, while the unchanged accepted
+  active graph contains six macOS-only schemes. Neither path is modified by this
+  candidate; the pre-existing cross-owner anomaly is recorded in `LOGBOOK.md`
+  and is not misreported as green or fixed.
+- Product Swift/Go builds: not rerun. The candidate changes documentation,
+  diagram source/render, README, logbook, and board outcomes only; it does not
+  change executable product or workflow code.
+
+## Acceptance mapping
+
+1. Contract §3 inventories each seed and required workflow trigger/job with
+   actor trust, input, permissions, environment/secrets, network, outputs,
+   retention, and approval.
+2. Contract §§2–3 deny PR production environments, production secrets/signing
+   material, write/publication authority, privileged runners, and trusted
+   release namespaces; token default is `contents: read` and otherwise none.
+3. Contract §§4–5 name nine exact blocking checks and map every CI requirement
+   to exactly one primary check plus macOS/iOS/relay/review ownership.
+4. Contract §§7–8 cover every required threat scenario and bind rejecting
+   fixtures to named downstream production call sites, including the observed
+   board-validator fail-open shape.
+5. Contract §9 keeps autonomous agent review binding for implementation and
+   human security/release/platform ratification accountable at
+   `TASK-260717-2d308k` before publication.
+
+## Board and decomposition audit
+
+No element or planning artifact was created. The existing smallest atomic owner
+set still covers policy, board/spec validation, Apple/Core/relay build gates,
+supply chain, versioning, orchestration, evidence, and adversarial verification.
+The exact spec omissions filled by the contract remain retention values,
+environment names, endpoint allowlists, and conditional SARIF scope; §9 records
+their justification and out-of-scope audit. No research question remains open.
+
+## Residual risks
+
+- Workflows and their negative fixtures remain downstream implementation work;
+  this task records the binding contract only.
+- Human ratification remains pending at `TASK-260717-2d308k` and blocks
+  publication, not downstream implementation of an agent-accepted draft.
+- `references/negative-evidence.md` remains unavailable, so its contents are
+  unknown; the contract does not infer constraints from its absence.
+- The pre-existing credential-free scheme-set regression test remains red under
+  its cross-owner scope and must not be treated as a pass.
