+
+## Acceptance mapping
+
+1. Contract §3 inventories each seed and required workflow trigger/job with
+   actor trust, input, permissions, environment/secrets, network, outputs,
+   retention, and approval.
+2. Contract §§2–3 deny PR production environments, production secrets/signing
+   material, write/publication authority, privileged runners, and trusted
+   release namespaces; token default is `contents: read` and otherwise none.
+3. Contract §§4–5 name nine exact blocking checks and map every CI requirement
+   to exactly one primary check plus macOS/iOS/relay/review ownership.
+4. Contract §§7–8 cover every required threat scenario and bind rejecting
+   fixtures to named downstream production call sites, including the observed
+   board-validator fail-open shape.
+5. Contract §9 keeps autonomous agent review binding for implementation and
+   human security/release/platform ratification accountable at
+   `TASK-260717-2d308k` before publication.
